<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean debt market closed for Liberation Day.</title>
<headline>S.Korean debt market closed for Liberation Day.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's debt market is closed on Friday for Liberation Day, a public holiday.</p>
<p>Benchmark three-year corporate bond yields closed higher on Thursday as fears continued over tightening short-term liquidity, dealers said.</p>
<p>* 3-yr corporates close at 12.15 pct vs Wednesday's 12.10.</p>
<p>* 3-mth CDs end at 12.60 pct vs 12.55.</p>
<p>* Overnight average call rate at 12.80 pct vs 12.60.</p>
<p>-- Yeom Yoon-jeong (822) 727 5647</p>
